From c6c600a13419c2966749b5687ca8b08d27b0e182 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:06:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pyluwen: tt-station broker backend (macOS); ARC queue: MSI
 doorbell, stale-reply drain, cross-process lock

- bind/pyluwen/src/ttstation_broker.rs: a luwen chip backend over tt-station's ttbh broker, for a
  Blackhole attached to a Mac over Thunderbolt (no tt-kmd). Opt-in via TTSTATION_BROKER. NOC
  read/write through one 2 MiB window; every MMIO access widened to aligned 32-bit (a 3-byte read
  of ARC_MISC_CNTL returned ffffff on the Mac).
- PciChip/pci_scan/detect_chips use it when enabled; PciBlackhole pci_board_type/pci_interface_id
  fall back to the backend's DeviceInfo.
- blackhole/message.rs: also ring the MSI catcher FIFO (tt-kmd's doorbell; fw bundle 19.2.0
  ignores irq0_trig), drain uncollected responses before sending (as tt-kmd does), and, when
  TTSTATION_BROKER is set, hold a file lock for the whole exchange (concurrent processes crossed
  replies without it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
